mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Common Thread Backend\n\nGoogle sign-in uses Internet Identity. Anonymous visitors may play static daily puzzles. Authenticated callers register a SHA-256 hash of a random service capability through openServiceSession(hash). Only the caller owns that hash; it expires after 30 minutes. checkServiceSession(hash) returns the matching principal only while valid. closeServiceSession(hash) revokes only the caller's session. The raw capability stays out of canister state. The Claude gateway verifies the mainnet query signature before using the principal to select private records.\n\nPersonal stories and learning topics are stored separately in owner-scoped service storage. Personal stories are never connected to learning topics. Subject and transcript generation have separate authority rules, with no automatic paid retries. The former anonymous generatePersonalPuzzle endpoint is disabled and never calls Caffeine Inference. AI credentials remain server-side.\n\nThe canister's OQL entity list is empty. Session records are not exposed through OQL. Caller roles remain supported for Caffeine compatibility; the portfolio visitor export is protected separately by the original service-owner identity and contains only optional contact details and aggregate signed-in account counts, never private story content.\n\nSaved accounts support export and deletion. A minimal deletion marker prevents automatic restoration by stale clients. Daily boards are browser-playable, with a fixed 365-combination schedule from reviewed connection groups, rotating at UTC midnight. Casual friend links contain puzzle answers and are not cheat-resistant or ranked."
  };
};
